Specifically:

* electrolites/kernels/cuda/gvhf-rys/*, electrolites/kernels/cuda/gint/*
  are copies of GPU4PySCF 1.7.0 sources, unmodified, and are compiled here
  only as support for the library below.

* electrolites/kernels/cuda/my1e/{g1e.cu, g1e_root_1.cu, g3c1e.cu,
  rys_roots.cu, constant.cu} are derived from the GPU4PySCF 1.8.1 files of
  the same names under lib/gint.  Three kinds of change: the far-field Boys
  and Rys path described in docs/README_fast1e.md (new headers
  gint1e_boys.cuh and gint1e_g1e_roots.cuh); the int3c1e kernels demoted from
  __global__ to __device__ so that int3c1e_wrappers.cu can give each angular
  -momentum class an extern "C" entry point NVRTC can name; and #include
  lines rewritten because NVRTC resolves them only against -I and has no
  <math.h>.  The declarations those includes used to bring in are reproduced
  in my1e/int3c1e_prologue.cuh, BasisProdCache verbatim -- fast1e.py copies
  GPU4PySCF's own instance of that struct into the kernels' __constant__, so
  the two definitions have to agree.  my1e/rys_tables.cuh replaces
  lib/gvhf-rys/rys_roots.cuh's extern arrays with pointers into the repacked
  tables below.

* electrolites/kernels/cuda/myk2/rys_k_general.cu is derived from
  GPU4PySCF's lib/gvhf-rys/rys_contract_k.cu.  One change is a bug fix
  upstream made independently in 1.8.0 (the gout_pattern bit shift, upstream
  PR #791); the rest is the restructuring described in docs/README_fastk.md.

* electrolites/kernels/cuda/gvhf-rys181/gvhf-rys/* are copies of GPU4PySCF
  **1.8.1** sources.  All but one are unmodified and are compiled here only as
  support for the library below; a 1.8.1 set is needed alongside the 1.7.0 one
  because BoundsInfo gained per-group q_cond/s_cond in between.  The exception
  is build_rys_gxyz.cuh, whose three per-Rys-root divisions are folded like the
  rest of the P1 treatment.  A second file, vhf.cuh, is modified only when the
  generator is asked for the register cap (--p3, which is measured not to pay
  and so is not the shipped configuration): its adjust_threads macro then has
  the register-driven thread doubling disabled, because with a cap in place
  that branch becomes reachable and could change the block shape out from under
  the launch bound.  docs/README_fastejk2.md 4 has the measurements.

* electrolites/kernels/cuda/myejk2/{rys_contract_jk_ip2.cu,
  unrolled_ejk_ip2_type12.cu, unrolled_ejk_ip2_type3.cu} are derived from the
  GPU4PySCF 1.8.1 files of the same names under lib/gvhf-rys, by
  codegen/gen_ejk_ip2.py.  Two changes, both described in
  docs/README_fastejk2.md: every double-precision division in the primitive and
  Rys-root loops becomes a multiply by a reciprocal formed once per primitive
  pair, and each kernel gains a __launch_bounds__.  The Rys recurrences, the
  per-atom contraction, the screening, the symmetry factors and the two extern
  "C" drivers are upstream's, unaltered apart from the entry-point names.

* electrolites/kernels/fastk_generated.cu and fastk2_generated.cu are emitted
  by codegen/gen_kernels.py and codegen/gen_k2_kernels.py, which lift the
  integral arithmetic of GPU4PySCF's lib/gvhf-rys/unrolled_rys_k.cu and
  restructure the code around it.  electrolites/kernels/fastj_generated.cu is
  emitted the same way from lib/gvhf-md/unrolled_md_j.cu.

* electrolites/kernels/fastjk_generated.cu and fastjk2_generated.cu are
  emitted the same way by codegen/gen_kernels.py --jk and
  codegen/gen_k2_kernels.py --jk, lifting the integral arithmetic and the
  fused J-and-K contraction of GPU4PySCF's lib/gvhf-rys/unrolled_rys_jk.cu.
  electrolites/kernels/fastjk_prologue.cu's fill_vjk_tasks/fill_vjk_tasks2
  reproduce the screening tests of that release's
  lib/gvhf-rys/create_tasks.cu _fill_vjk_tasks for a 1D and a 2D thread block.

* electrolites/kernels/fastkhigh_generated.cu, fastjkhigh_generated.cu and
  fastejk_generated.cu are written from the angular-momentum class alone by
  codegen/gen_khigh.py (with and without --jk) and codegen/gen_ejk.py; no
  GPU4PySCF source is used as input for them.  They do follow GPU4PySCF's
  screening tests, task ordering and symmetry factors, and the fused ones
  follow the index order of its two Coulomb contractions, which is
  load-bearing at hermi = 0.

* electrolites/kernels/data/rys_roots_dat.npz holds the Rys root and weight
  tables of GPU4PySCF's lib/gvhf-rys/rys_roots_dat.cu, repacked.

* electrolites/fastfnlc.py's _nr_rks_fnlc_mo is derived from GPU4PySCF
  1.8.1's hessian/rks.py nr_rks_fnlc_mo.  Two changes, both described in
  docs/README_fastfnlc.md: the ground-state half is factored into
  _ground_state and memoised on the orbitals it depends on, and the
  potential contraction is batched over the perturbed densities.  Every
  libgdft call, the VV10 parameters, the grid, the zero-density threshold and
  the factors are upstream's, unaltered.

* electrolites/compat.py's tril_pair_mappings is GPU4PySCF 1.7.0's
  jk._make_tril_pair_mappings, vendored because 1.8.0 removed it while the
  kernels here still consume its output.

The screening criteria, the Rys quadrature and the density-matrix contraction
symmetry factors are GPU4PySCF's throughout, which is why a patched run
reproduces an unpatched one to round-off.  See docs/UPGRADE_1.8.1.md for the
measured agreement.
